<title>ALGERIA: Algiers building company loses $2.2 million.</title>
<headline>Algiers building company loses $2.2 million.</headline>
<dateline>ALGIERS 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Algiers building company ECA (l&quot;Entreprise de Construction d'Alger) made a loss of 128 million dinars ($2.2 million) in 1996 , the official news agency APS said on Monday.</p>
<p>The loss was recorded on a turnover of 2.09 billion dinars.</p>
<p>Another public works company, ER Barika (l'Entreprise de Realisation de Barika), made an after tax profit of 5.8 million dinars ($105,260), the agency said. Barika lies some 225 km (140 miles) southeast of Algiers.</p>
<p>($1= 56 dinars)</p>
</text>
